+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Writes src/static_page.baked.tsx: a first screen of about 1,000 nodes whose
+JSX is written out element by element (no loop), like a hand-written content
+screen (terms, onboarding, a settings page). Used to measure what a
+build-time-only subtree saves (REPORT-13-cold-start.md).
+
+  tools/gen-static-page.py [cards=90] > src/static_page.baked.tsx
+"""
+import sys
+
+cards = int(sys.argv[1]) if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 90
+COLORS = ["#3366ff", "#2e9e5b", "#e08a00", "#d64545", "#7a4fd6", "#0aa5a5", "#c2478f", "#5b6b7a"]
+TOPICS = ["Account", "Privacy", "Notifications", "Storage", "Appearance", "Language", "Security", "Billing", "Help", "About"]
+out = []
+out.append("// Generated by tools/gen-static-page.py. %d cards of 11 nodes, written out literally." % cards)
+out.append('import { View, Text, ScrollView } from "solid-fuse";')
+out.append("")
+out.append("export default function StaticPage() {")
+out.append("  return (")
+out.append("    <ScrollView>")
+out.append("      <View padding={16}>")
+for i in range(cards):
+    topic = TOPICS[i % len(TOPICS)]
+    out.append("""        <View
+          padding={{ horizontal: 16, vertical: 10 }}
+          margin={{ bottom: 8 }}
+          decoration={{ color: "#ffffff", borderRadius: 12, border: { width: 1, color: "#e2e2e2" } }}
+          flex={{ direction: "horizontal", gap: 12, align: "center" }}
+        >
+          <View width={40} height={40} alignment="center" decoration={{ color: "%s", shape: "circle" }}>
+            <Text color="white" fontWeight="bold">%s</Text>
+          </View>
+          <View flex={{ gap: 2 }}>
+            <Text fontSize={16} fontWeight="semiBold">%s settings, section %d</Text>
+            <Text fontSize={13} color="#666666" maxLines={1} overflow="ellipsis">What section %d of %s controls, in one line</Text>
+          </View>
+          <Text fontSize={12} color="#999999">%d items</Text>
+        </View>""" % (COLORS[i % 8], topic[0], topic, i + 1, i + 1, topic.lower(), 3 + i % 7))
+out.append("      </View>")
+out.append("    </ScrollView>")
+out.append("  );")
+out.append("}")
+print("\n".join(out))
diff --git a/packages/docs/content/docs/architecture.mdx b/packages/docs/content/docs/architecture.mdx
index 2e33044..586c496 100644
--- a/packages/docs/content/docs/architecture.mdx
+++ b/packages/docs/content/docs/architecture.mdx
@@ -63,3 +63,12 @@ One package manager for both sides.
 **Development** — `fuse dev` starts Vite and Flutter together. Dart connects to the Vite dev server via WebSocket, pre-fetches ES modules, and evaluates them in FJS. HMR works — edit, save, see it on device.
 
 **Production** — `fuse build` produces a single IIFE bundle with optional bytecode compilation. The Dart layer is a stable native SDK that rarely changes. The JS bundle is where product code lives and can ship continuously — including over-the-air without app store review.
+
+### Startup (experimental)
+
+These exist to measure what a build step can take off app startup (`examples/perf_bench/REPORT-13-cold-start.md`). They are prototypes: off by default, and their names and behaviour will change.
+
+- **Bytecode as an asset.** By default a release app compiles the bundle to QuickJS bytecode on first launch and caches it in the documents directory. Setting `QuickJsConnection.bytecodeAsset = 'assets/js/bundle.bc'` before `start()` loads bytecode the build shipped instead: the source is not read, hashed or compiled on the device. The bytecode must be produced by the same QuickJS build as the engine in the app; if the engine rejects it, the source bundle is used.
+- **Prerendered first screen.** `fuse build --prerender` runs the bundle at build time and writes the op batch of its first screen to `assets/js/prerender.json`. `FuseRuntime.deferred()` creates a runtime without loading the engine, and `runtime.applyPrerendered(json)` builds the node tree from that batch, so `runApp` can show the screen before JS has started. When JS delivers its own first batch, `FuseTakeover.hydrate` keeps the nodes (nothing is rebuilt if the batch is identical; differing props and texts are patched; a different structure is remounted), `FuseTakeover.remount` replaces them, and `FuseTakeover.trust` lets JS skip sending the batch when its op and node counts match. Events on the prerendered screen are dropped unless `runtime.replayEarlyEvents` is set. The build-time render knows nothing about the device: screen size, theme, locale, stored state and anything fetched are whatever the build assumed.
+- **Baked subtrees.** A module named `*.baked.tsx` whose default export is a component without props is rendered by `fuse build`; its nodes go to `assets/js/baked.json` and the module becomes a stub that emits one op. Register the shapes before `start()` with `runtime.registerBaked(...)`. Nothing inside a baked subtree can be updated from JS or carry an event handler. In `fuse dev` the module is an ordinary component.
+
